        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "i.e. each block is reduced to an estimate of a central subspace that carries all the information that block holds about the other block. In sample, with the independence conditions relaxed to zero covariance, Cook et al. (2023) estimate the two subspaces by a pair of PLS-type deflation loops, one per block. Let  $ \\mathbf{X}_0 = \\mathbf{X} $ and  $ \\mathbf{Y}_0 = \\mathbf{Y} $; the weight vectors maximize the covariance between a candidate score in the (deflated) own block and the other block in full,",
            "block_bbox": [
                136,
                528,
                1083,
                676
            ],
            "block_id": 5,
            "block_order": 6,
            "group_id": 5,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    136.0,
                    528.0
                ],
                [
                    1083.0,
                    528.0
                ],
                [
                    1083.0,
                    676.0
                ],
                [
                    136.0,
                    676.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "display_formula",
            "block_content": " $$ w_{i}=\\underset{\\|c\\|=1}{\\operatorname{argmax}}\\ \\mathbf{c}^{\\top}\\mathbf{X}_{i-1}^{\\top}\\mathbf{Y}\\mathbf{Y}^{\\top}\\mathbf{X}_{i-1}\\mathbf{c},\\quad\\mathbf{t}_{i}=\\mathbf{X}_{i-1}w_{i}, $$ ",
