        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "Two features matter downstream. First, the reduction is genuinely multivariate: a single joint model relates all $p$ predictors to all $q$ responses through a shared low-dimensional score space. Second, Serneels (2025) has extended the extraction with soft-thresholding on $\\boldsymbol{w}$ and $\\boldsymbol{v}$, governed by penalties $\\eta_{x}, \\eta_{y} \\in [0,1)$. This produces a sparse, variable-selecting variant, which was first in its kind to produce dimension reduction in which both the number of components and the sparsity can be tuned individually in each block. It is noted that a huge literature exists on sufficient variable selection (see e.g. Menvouta et al. (2022) for",
